renuous but unsuccessful effort to bring back the ten tribes to their allegiance.","verses":20,"father":"Rehoboam","mother":"Maachah","v":[1]},{"id":"benjamin_463","name":"Benjamin","also":"Ben-oni","summary":"The younger son of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 35:18). His birth took place at Ephrath, on the road between Bethel and Bethlehem, at a short distance from the latter place.","verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[8]},{"id":"zerah_3046","name":"Zerah","also":"","summary":"An “Ethiopian,” probably Osorkon II., the successor of Shishak on the throne of Egypt. With an enormous army, the largest we read of in Scripture, he invaded the kingdom of Judah in the days of Asa (2 Chr. 14:9-15).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9]}],"places":[{"id":"mareshah_767","name":"Mareshah","kind":"City","lat":31.59296,"lon":34.89824,"summary":"Possession, a city in the plain of Judah (John. 15:44). Here Asa defeated Zerah the Ethiopian (2 Chr. 14:9, 10).","verses":6,"v":[9,10]},{"id":"valley_of_zephathah_1223","name":"valley of Zephathah","kind":"Valley","lat":31.6152,"lon":34.91009,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[10]},{"id":"gerar_459","name":"Gerar","kind":"City","lat":31.38176,"lon":34.60698,"summary":"A region; lodging-place, a very ancient town and district in the south border of Palestine, which was ruled over by a king named Abimelech (Gen. 10:19; 20:1, 2).","verses":9,"v":[13,14]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[15]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[29,29,7901,5973,1,1,6912,6912,6912,5892,5892,5892,1732,1732,1121,1121,1121,609,4427,8478,8478,8478,3117,3117,3117,3117,776,776,8252,8252,8252,6235,6235,8141],[609,609,6213,2896,2896,2896,3477,3477,5869,5869,5869,3068,3068,3068,430,